// Types whose values are in an order, as for sorting. The numbers, `char`, and `String` are
// comparable without implementing it: they have a `compareTo` of their own, and satisfy a
// `T extends Comparable<T>` bound. `float` and `double` are in a total order, as in Java: -0 sorts
// before 0, and NaN after every other value and the same as any other NaN.

interface Comparable<T> {
    // Negative, zero, or positive as this value sorts before, the same as, or after `other`.
    readonly int compareTo(T other);
}
